# data (large, not committed — see README for how to reconstruct)
/data/
# Two exceptions live under /data/ despite the rule above:
#   data/splits/*.txt        — which videos are train/val/test/background
#   data/gold_test/annotations.json — the human-labeled gold ground truth
# Both are small, essential reproducibility artifacts, not "data" in the
# large/regenerable sense this rule is for. NOTE (corrected 2026-09-12):
# `!` negation patterns do NOT un-ignore a path under an already-ignored
# parent directory in this git version — confirmed by testing, despite
# looking like it worked once a file was already tracked (git stops
# applying .gitignore to a path the moment it's tracked, which is a
# different mechanism and misled the first version of this comment).
# The actual fix is `git add -f` when adding these two file patterns —
# there is no way to make plain .gitignore rules do this cleanly here.
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mov
*.zip

# model weights / checkpoints
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine

# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.venv/
venv/

# OS
.DS_Store

# large generated results (plots/tables/logs stay tracked, videos/checkpoints don't)
results/**/*.mp4
results/**/*.avi

# regenerable review-image dumps from any method's eval/labeling run
# (bulky; the JSON predictions/annotations + manifests are the tracked
# deliverable, not the images — regenerate by rerunning the method)
results/pseudo_labels/frames/
results/**/review/
